-- title:
--   Quotient of a complete regular local domain by a regular parameter
-- statement:
--   Let $R$ be a commutative ring which is a domain, which is a regular local ring and a regular ring, and which is complete (and separated) for the $\mathfrak m$-adic topology, $\mathfrak m =$ `maximalIdeal R`; let $x \in R$ satisfy $x \in \mathfrak m$, $x \notin \mathfrak m^2$ and $x \neq 0$, and assume the quotient $R / (x)$ by the ideal generated by $x$ is local. Then five assertions hold simultaneously: $R/(x)$ is a regular local ring; $R/(x)$ is a domain; the Krull dimensions satisfy $\dim (R/(x)) + 1 = \dim R$ as elements of `ringKrullDim`'s value type (i.e. in $\mathbb{Z} \cup \{\pm\infty\}$ with the order-theoretic conventions of `ringKrullDim`); $R/(x)$ is complete for the adic topology of its own maximal ideal; and the maximal ideal of $R/(x)$ is the image of $\mathfrak m$ under the quotient map $R \to R/(x)$, so that the residue fields of $R$ and of $R/(x)$ coincide.
--
--   This is the standard statement that cutting a complete regular local domain by a regular parameter $x \in \mathfrak m \setminus \mathfrak m^2$ again yields a complete regular local domain, of dimension one smaller and with the same residue field. It is used in the construction of discrete valuation rings dominating complete local rings of Krull dimension at most two, which in turn serves the deformation-theoretic part of the modularity lifting argument.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_IsRegularLocalRing_quotient_span_singleton_isAdicComplete_of_notMem_sq.lean

import Mathlib

